WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.259 --> 00:00:03.540
(whimsical music)

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.740
- [Sharon] Say you've
been caring for an animal

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.150
and you actually do have to
do that little bit of syringe

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.987
feeding, and then the next
day you go in there to syringe

00:00:09.987 --> 00:00:11.290
feed it, and it wants to eat you,

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.890
you know you've done a good job.

00:00:14.218 --> 00:00:16.210
(telephone ringing)

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.490
- Good afternoon,
Tiggywinkles, Alyssa speaking,

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.367
how can I help?

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.940
(playful music)

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.336
- Welcome to Tiggywinkles,

00:00:23.336 --> 00:00:25.190
the world's busiest wildlife hospital.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.000
- [Narrator] Meet Sharon Jacobs.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.333
She's a senior nurse here at Tiggywinkles.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.450
This adorable wildlife hospital
is named after a character

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.730
from the Beatrix Potter children's book,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.903
Mrs. Tiggy-Winkle.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.500
But this isn't a place
you take your sick dog

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.310
like Florence the British Bulldog.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.790
Right, Flo?
(barking)

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.870
This is for all wild
animals found injured.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.560
X-rays taken.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.340
- [Sharon] We deal with
all British wildlife

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.850
as in foxes, badgers, deer, wood mice.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.710
- [Narrator] They treat
rabbits, bats, big birds,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.740
small birds, and very,
very cute hedgehogs.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.573
Oh, just look at him swimming.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.820
They get around 10,000 animals
through the door each year

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.350
with a wide range of
sicknesses and injuries.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.023
- OK, this guy came into
us about two weeks ago, and

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:14.670
she fractured her tibia,

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.100
so we've actually put Plaster of Paris on,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.600
which is a cast.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.270
- [Narrator] The wildlife
hospital is just like a human one.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.810
Luckily for the animals,
there isn't a waiting room.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.140
- Any animal that comes through the door

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.290
the first thing is they
do they go for a triage.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:29.080
So, and literally, they are
medically assessed there;

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.210
see if there's any injuries;
see if they need a drip;

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.720
see if they need any antibiotics,

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.120
painkillers and stuff like that.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.500
Within 24 hours they normally
get reassessed by the vet

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.530
and any sort of like
medical treatment or wounds

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.790
or injuries or x-rays when
you think is normally done.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.820
Then, once the animal is fully fit,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.770
as in medically inside
we want it to go outside.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.900
So if it's a bird for argument's sake

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:48.870
it would go into an aviary.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.710
If it was a deer it would
go down our paddocks

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.500
and again once we're happy with them

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.280
then the aim is to get
everything back to the wild.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.723
We don't keep anything 'cause
it looks cute and fluffy.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.773
It is quite nice

00:01:59.773 --> 00:02:01.900
when it comes to actually
releasing the animal

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.230
and now and again some
of the deer will actually

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.009
bolt off and then turn around
and stare at you goin',

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:08.340
what's goin' on here?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.980
So it's quite nice.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.240
I think the aim of Tiggywinkles

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.980
is obviously to save the animal's life

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.270
but also to educate people
about how to treat them,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.230
how to get the animal back to the wild.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.280
If you do see an animal that's injured

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.960
do take it to a wildlife hospital.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.330
- [Narrator] So it can get better

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.960
and that way this little fella

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.034
could rest up with his cast.

00:02:28.034 --> 00:02:30.701
(playful music)

00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:37.562
(electronic chiming)

